endobj

251 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 102 0 R/T(ESG Framework & Materiality)/E(ESG Framework & Materiality)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

252 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 102 0 R/E(O\220Reilly\220s ESG profile is evaluated using a materiality-based framework that focuses on factors most likely to influence long-term financial performance and risk. In the automotive aftermarket, material ESG considerations include supply chain emissions, labor practices, customer safety, and governance structures that support disciplined capital allocation. Rather than treating ESG as a standalone objective, these factors are assessed based on their impact on operational resilience, cost structure, and execution risk.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

253 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 102 0 R/T(Environmental Factors)/E(Environmental Factors)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

254 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 102 0 R/T(Social Factors)/E(Social Factors)/Pg 12 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 102 0 R/E(Social considerations for O\220Reilly center on workforce management, employee retention, and customer service quality in a labor-intensive retail environment. The company\220s workforce metrics are broadly in line with industry averages, with no material labor controversies reported. Stable employee retention and strong relationships with professional installers support consistent service levels and customer loyalty. In addition, O\220Reilly\220s emphasis on safety training and in-store service standards mitigates operational and reputational risk.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 102 0 R/T(Governance Factors)/E(Governance Factors)/Pg 12 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 102 0 R/E(O\220Reilly exhibits strong governance practices supported by an independent and experienced board, well-defined committee oversight, and executive compensation structures aligned with long-term performance. Governance strength is particularly evident in the company\220s disciplined capital allocation strategy, which prioritizes high-return reinvestment and shareholder value creation. Transparent disclosure practices and internal controls further reduce governance-related risk and support consistent execution across economic cycles.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

