527 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 113 0 R/T(To supplement our intrinsic valuation, we conducted a relative valuation analysis using a focused peer set of publicly traded U.S. automotive aftermarket retailers with comparable business models and end-market exposure. The peer group includes AutoZone and Genuine Parts Company, which represent the most relevant public comparables to O\220Reilly Automotive. Advance Auto Parts is excluded from certain metrics due to negative EBITDA, which renders EV-based multiples not meaningful.)/E(To supplement our intrinsic valuation, we conducted a relative valuation analysis using a focused peer set of publicly traded U.S. automotive aftermarket retailers with comparable business models and end-market exposure. The peer group includes AutoZone and Genuine Parts Company, which represent the most relevant public comparables to O\220Reilly Automotive. Advance Auto Parts is excluded from certain metrics due to negative EBITDA, which renders EV-based multiples not meaningful.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[2 3]>>
endobj

528 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 113 0 R/T(Relative valuation metrics are sourced from publicly available market data and applied consistently across the peer group. We evaluate valuation primarily using trailing P/E multiples, which provide a conservative equity-level cross-check to our discounted cash flow analysis. Implied valuation ranges are calculated by applying observed peer multiples to O\220Reilly\220s forecasted financial metrics, as detailed in the accompanying Excel model.)/E(Relative valuation metrics are sourced from publicly available market data and applied consistently across the peer group. We evaluate valuation primarily using trailing P/E multiples, which provide a conservative equity-level cross-check to our discounted cash flow analysis. Implied valuation ranges are calculated by applying observed peer multiples to O\220Reilly\220s forecasted financial metrics, as detailed in the accompanying Excel model.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[4 5]>>
endobj

